<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdallah Jamma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdallah Jamma was the leader of the Qawasma <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> around 1500. In alliance with the Funj leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amara-dunqas">Amara Dunqas</a> he destroyed the Christian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alodia">Alodia</a> and its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soba">Soba</a>. He founded the Abdallab Sheikhdom with its seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qerri">Qerri</a>, and his descendants ruled the northern Sudanese Nile as the chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Funj Sultanate of Sennar</a>.</p></div>
